.TH PolyTabletop 1 "2026" "polytabletop 0.9" "Jocuri de masa"
.SH NAME
polytabletop \- table-top games (171 clean-room games) in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polytabletop list
.br
.B polytabletop catalog
.RB [ \-\-kind " implemented|traditional|branded|toolkit]"
.br
.B polytabletop play
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-you " one|two|both|none]" 
.RB [ \-\-seed " N]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
PolyTabletop is a clean-room Rust implementation of table-top games. The computer plays the other seats.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Print the id, title and rules summary of every playable game.
.TP
.B catalog
Print the whole target catalog with the status of each entry; \fB\-\-kind\fR filters by status.
.TP
.B play ID
Play game ID. You are Player 1 unless \fB\-\-you\fR says otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-you " one|two|both|none"
Which seat(s) are human. \fBboth\fR is hot-seat; \fBnone\fR watches the AI play itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Make deals, dice and AI choices reproducible.
.SH IN-GAME COMMANDS
Type a move (for example \fBe2e4\fR, \fBc3xe5\fR, \fBd6\fR). \fB?\fR lists legal moves, \fBhint\fR asks the AI for a suggestion, \fBq\fR quits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POLYTABLETOP_AI_MS
Time budget in milliseconds for the search AI.
.SH FILES
Completions: completions/polytabletop.bash, completions/_polytabletop, completions/polytabletop.fish.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR polytabletop-gui (1),
.BR polytabletop-rpg (1)
